v 3
d surveymap: map how respondents moved through a survey
d
d surveymap reads a survey dataset in memory -- one row per respondent,
d columns in questionnaire order -- and maps the flow: who was asked each
d item, who answered, who was routed around it by skip logic (read from the
d responses themselves), and who declined.  Declared or detected branching
d variables split the flow into lanes with counts and percentages on every
d box and connector; small noisy branches pool into "other" under prune
d rules you can change without rescanning.
d
d Outputs, all built from one journal file: a Results-window receipt, a
d self-contained HTML flow map (no internet, no JavaScript), mermaid text,
d and an Excel tracker whose sheets can sit inside a datadictionary
d codebook workbook.
d
d Start with: surveymap demo
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Author: Eric Booth
d Support: email eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d
